00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.730
So here I’ve got a really nice sample of
silicon, alright?

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:03.730
Ok.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:07.090
I’m going to take it out of the bottle…
of the… I’m going to

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.160
have to wash my hands after this.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.719
So silicon is a very common element, it’s
particularly found in

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:18.540
sand which is the oxide of silica; that’s
the compound of

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.610
oxygen and silicon.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:30.740
It is also found in a variety of minerals
which contain silicon,

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.450
oxygen and another metal which are known as
silicates. And

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.890
silicates occur in an enormous number of different
minerals.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.789
It’s sort of the part of science that unless
you are a specialist

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:47.850
you find quite boring but if you really go
into it like everything

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.039
else it becomes really quite interesting.

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:53.429
So this is a piece of polycrystalline silicon.
It’s a really quite

00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:57.050
fantastic element and it’s very often used,
or in fact it’s used

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.679
very regularly to make electronic components.
All of the

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:02.199
computers that we use and actually the camera
that you are

00:01:02.199 --> 00:01:05.790
recording me on now are based upon silicon
technology.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:10.250
Silicon is also extremely important and the
basis of most of

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:16.220
the electronic devices we use: my watch, your
video camera,

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:23.070
and also in computers. And if we look over
here, I have got

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:27.830
here this is an example of a silicon wafer;
you can see at the

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:30.960
back this is silicon.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.640
So the silicon is grown as a single crystal
from which we can

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.000
make very highly-refined architectures on
silicon chips, but

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.590
you see here we have a polycrystalline sample
so it is very

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:43.641
pretty the way that it interacts with the
light and you can see

00:01:43.641 --> 00:01:45.920
the different grain sizes.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.700
So let me take it out.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.730
Did Martyn show you the single crystal, the
wafer?

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:51.790
Yeah, he’s got a single chip, yeah, yeah.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:54.010
Cause if you can get the light coming off
it, you can get all

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.780
sorts of different coloured affects.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.570
Here you can see, this is pure silicon on
the back and on the

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:06.770
front, people have grown chips these are the
Pentium 4 chips

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:12.069
for the computer, I think, I am not absolutely
sure but I think

00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:14.540
these are the chips and these are the connectors
on either

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:18.400
side. So there are a whole lot of these chips
and they grow a

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.409
large number of them at once. These are chopped
up and

00:02:21.409 --> 00:02:25.120
tested and the ones that worked are put into
computers and

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.560
the ones that are no good are just chucked
and so this is a

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:35.920
fantastically delicate piece of engineering
making these. This

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:41.360
is so-called 20cm wafer. They now make silicon
chips on a

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.120
30cm wafer which is about this size and you
can get a large

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.719
number more on them.

00:02:47.719 --> 00:02:50.939
If you get a single crystal of this silicon
structure, it can

00:02:50.939 --> 00:02:53.110
diffract the light and change the light so
that it diffracts and

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.329
bends off at different angles so that you
get like a rainbow

00:02:55.329 --> 00:02:57.659
effect off it. It’s really quite beautiful.

00:02:57.659 --> 00:03:03.469
A compound of silicon, silicon nitride is
extremely tough and

00:03:03.469 --> 00:03:08.629
very light so it’s very difficult to break
and silicon nitride for

00:03:08.629 --> 00:03:14.690
example is used in the impellers in turbo
chargers in cars. So

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.909
when you put your foot down on the accelerator
it will spin

00:03:17.909 --> 00:03:22.891
up very fast because it is very light but
it is very strong so it

00:03:22.891 --> 00:03:26.349
won’t very suddenly fall to bits as it is
revving up inside your

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:27.689
engine.

00:03:27.689 --> 00:03:29.131
Right I must put that there because I want
to put that back

00:03:29.131 --> 00:03:29.709
in a bag.

